    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n21742" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">immŏdestĭa</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inm-</span></b> ), ae, f.
		immodestus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>intemperate conduct</i>, <i>immodesty</i>, <i>licentiousness</i> (very rare; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">not in Cic.): heri haec immodestia me
					coëgit, qui, etc.,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Am. 1, 1, 9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">publicanorum,</span>”
				<i>avarice</i>, <i>extortion</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 13, 50</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">histrionum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 14</span></i>
			.</div>
